      "message": "Among the issues with this approach (maybe someone has an idea): This is the only thing I know of that mutates the Settings as part of the parse + compile. That\u0027s bizarre - it\u0027s a setting that\u0027s designed to be generated, not consumed. (But it\u0027s also then referenced later during the compile ... so it\u0027s both).\n\nIn theory, this should emit a ProgramElement for the version directive, but we need to keep referring to it, so having (at least) a copy of the version in the Settings seems like it makes sense?\n\nAs it stands, it will be lost when you call description() on the Program - I can go back and add code to re-emit the directive based on the settings, but again - if there were a ProgramElement, that would happen naturally. 😕",
